  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of accountability mechanisms for Sudan operation through collective complaints and community feedback mechanisms</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is part of the special AAP envelope in the current UFE round. It aims to enhance Accountability to Affected Populations (AAP) among humanitarian actors in Sudan by strengthening and expanding complaints and feedback mechanisms (CFM). As a result, this project fosters a people-centred approach where communities are listened to, engaged and participate in all decisions affecting their lives, along with empowering people with specific needs, particularly women-led groups. This project provides safe, accessible, confidential two-ways communication channels between humanitarian actors and affected people, so they are positioned as partners, decision makers and stakeholders throughout humanitarian planning and response. UNICEF targets a combined total of 975,590 affected people with Protection sector activities.</narrative>
  </description>
